    front_text: 'What is the "Dawn Phenomenon" vs "Somogyi Effect" in diabetes?',
    back_text: 'DAWN PHENOMENON:\n- Early morning hyperglycemia (4-8 AM)\n- Caused by normal hormone release (cortisol, growth hormone)\n- Occurs WITHOUT nocturnal hypoglycemia\n- Treatment: Adjust evening insulin timing/dose\n\nSOMOGYI EFFECT (Rebound Hyperglycemia):\n- Morning hyperglycemia FOLLOWING nocturnal hypoglycemia\n- Body releases counter-regulatory hormones in response to low glucose\n- Patient may wake with sweating, nightmares\n- Treatment: Reduce evening insulin or add bedtime snack\n\nHOW TO DIFFERENTIATE:\n- Check blood glucose at 2-3 AM\n- Dawn: Normal/high at 3 AM\n- Somogyi: Low at 3 AM',
