    front_text: 'What is Charcot foot (neuropathic arthropathy)?',
    back_text: 'CHARCOT FOOT:\nProgressive destruction of bones/joints in insensate foot\n\nETIOLOGY:\n- Loss of protective sensation (neuropathy)\n- Repetitive microtrauma\n- Continued weight bearing on injured foot\n- Inflammation leads to bone destruction\n\nPRESENTATION:\n- Acute: Red, hot, swollen foot (mimics infection)\n- Chronic: Deformity, "rocker-bottom" foot\n- Midfoot most commonly affected\n- May have minimal pain despite severe damage\n\nDIAGNOSIS:\n- Clinical exam + imaging\n- X-ray: Bone destruction, fragmentation, dislocation\n\nTREATMENT:\n- Immobilization (total contact cast)\n- Non-weight bearing initially\n- Gradual return to protected weight bearing\n- Custom footwear/orthotics long-term\n\nKEY: High index of suspicion in diabetic with swollen foot',
    source_pdf_id: null,
    source_page_number: null,
