    front_text: 'What lab values are used to assess thyroid function?',
    back_text: 'TSH (Thyroid Stimulating Hormone):\n- Most sensitive screening test\n- Normal: 0.4-4.0 mU/L\n- Elevated in HYPOthyroidism\n- Decreased in HYPERthyroidism\n\nFREE T4 (Thyroxine):\n- Normal: 0.8-1.8 ng/dL\n- Decreased in hypothyroidism\n- Elevated in hyperthyroidism\n\nFREE T3 (Triiodothyronine):\n- More active hormone\n- Used to confirm hyperthyroidism\n\nINTERPRETATION:\n\nHYPOTHYROIDISM:\n- TSH HIGH, T4 LOW (primary)\n- TSH normal/low, T4 LOW (secondary - pituitary)\n\nHYPERTHYROIDISM:\n- TSH LOW, T4 HIGH (primary)\n- TSH HIGH, T4 HIGH (secondary - rare)',
