    front_text: 'What is the difference between Sensitivity and Specificity?',
    back_text: 'SENSITIVITY (SnOut):\n- Identifies TRUE POSITIVES\n- Few false negatives\n- High sensitivity RULES OUT condition\n- "Sensitive tests detect disease"\n\nSPECIFICITY (SpIn):\n- Identifies TRUE NEGATIVES\n- Few false positives\n- High specificity RULES IN condition\n- "Specific tests confirm disease"',
    source_pdf_id: null,
    source_page_number: null,
    tags: ['sensitivity', 'specificity'],
  },
  {
    id: 'fc-research-3',
    subcategory_id: 'research-stats',
    front_text: 'What is the difference between Type I and Type II errors?',
    back_text: 'Type I Error (Alpha, α):\n- FALSE POSITIVE\n- Incorrectly reject true null hypothesis\n- "Finding something that isn\'t there"\n\nType II Error (Beta, β):\n- FALSE NEGATIVE\n- Incorrectly accept false null hypothesis\n- "Missing something that is there"',
    source_pdf_id: null,
    source_page_number: null,
    tags: ['type I error', 'type II error'],
  },
  {
    id: 'fc-research-4',
    subcategory_id: 'research-stats',
    front_text: 'What are the levels of measurement data?',
    back_text: 'NOMINAL (Qualitative): Categories, no order\n- Blood type, gender\n\nORDINAL (Qualitative): Rank order, no equal intervals\n- MMT grades, assistance levels\n\nINTERVAL (Quantitative): Equal intervals, no true zero\n- Temperature, IQ\n\nRATIO (Quantitative): Equal intervals, true zero\n- Height, weight, age (highest level)',
    source_pdf_id: null,
    source_page_number: null,
    tags: ['data types', 'measurement'],
  },
  {
    id: 'fc-research-5',
    subcategory_id: 'research-stats',
    front_text: 'What is the difference between Reliability and Validity?',
    back_text: 'RELIABILITY: Consistency of measurement\n- Intra-rater: Same person, multiple times\n- Inter-rater: Different people\n- Test-retest: Same test, different occasions\n\nVALIDITY: Measures what it claims to measure\n- Face: Subjective, weakest\n- Content: Covers the domain\n- Construct: Measures the concept\n- Criterion/Concurrent: Compared to gold standard, strongest',
    source_pdf_id: null,
    source_page_number: null,
    tags: ['reliability', 'validity'],
