    id: 'fc-equip-7',
    subcategory_id: 'equip-weight-bearing',
    front_text: 'What are the weight bearing status classifications?',
    back_text: 'WEIGHT BEARING STATUS:\n\nNWB (Non-Weight Bearing):\n- 0% weight on affected limb\n- Limb cannot touch ground\n- 3-point gait with walker/crutches\n\nTTWB (Toe Touch Weight Bearing):\n- Touch toe for balance only\n- No significant weight (5-10%)\n- Toe touches but no weight transfer\n\nPWB (Partial Weight Bearing):\n- Usually 25-50% body weight\n- Often specified by % or pounds\n- May use scale to practice\n\nWBAT (Weight Bearing As Tolerated):\n- Progress as comfort allows\n- Can bear full weight if tolerated\n- Patient determines amount\n\nFWB (Full Weight Bearing):\n- 100% weight allowed\n- Normal gait pattern\n- May still use device for safety',
    source_pdf_id: null,
    source_page_number: null,
    tags: ['weight bearing', 'status'],
