    back_text: '4-POINT GAIT:\n- PWB both legs\n- Poor balance/coordination\n- Bilateral weakness\n- Example: Parkinson disease\n\n2-POINT GAIT:\n- PWB both legs\n- Better balance than 4-point\n- Faster, more normal pattern\n- Example: Bilateral hip OA\n\n3-POINT GAIT:\n- NWB or PWB one leg\n- Requires good UE strength\n- Fractures, post-surgery\n- Example: S/P hip replacement (PWB)\n\nSWING-TO GAIT:\n- NWB both legs\n- Paralysis (SCI)\n- Slower, more stable\n\nSWING-THROUGH GAIT:\n- NWB both legs\n- Paralysis with good UE strength\n- Fastest, most efficient\n- High energy cost\n- Example: Paraplegia',
