    back_text: 'AXILLARY CRUTCH FITTING:\n\nHEIGHT:\n- Standing: 2-3 finger widths (1.5-2 inches) below axilla\n- Crutch length: Patient height minus 16 inches\n- Tips 4-6 inches lateral and 2 inches anterior to foot\n\nHANDGRIP:\n- At level of greater trochanter\n- OR at wrist crease when arms at side\n- Elbow flexion: 20-30 degrees\n\nCRITICAL POINTS:\n- Weight on HANDS, not axilla\n- Axillary pressure causes:\n  * Crutch palsy (radial nerve)\n  * Brachial plexus compression\n  * Vascular compromise\n\nSAFETY:\n- Rubber tips in good condition\n- Check tightness of hardware\n- Proper body mechanics\n\nSTAIRS:\n- UP: Good leg first ("up with the good")\n- DOWN: Crutches + affected leg first ("down with the bad")',
    source_pdf_id: null,
    source_page_number: null,
    tags: ['crutches', 'fitting', 'axillary'],
