    back_text: 'CANE TYPES:\n\n1. STANDARD/SINGLE-POINT CANE:\n- Most common\n- Minimal support\n- Used for balance, mild gait deviation\n\n2. OFFSET CANE:\n- Handle offset over shaft\n- Better weight distribution\n- Reduces wrist strain\n\n3. QUAD CANE (NARROW BASE):\n- 4 small feet\n- More stability than standard\n- Slower gait\n\n4. QUAD CANE (WIDE BASE):\n- 4 larger feet, wider base\n- Maximum stability\n- For significant balance deficits\n- Slowest gait\n\nFITTING:\n- Top at greater trochanter or wrist crease\n- Elbow flexion 20-30 degrees\n\nUSE:\n- Hold OPPOSITE affected leg\n- Advance with or slightly before affected leg\n- Creates wider BOS, reduces hip stress',
    source_pdf_id: null,
