    back_text: 'LOFSTRAND/FOREARM CRUTCHES:\n\nDESIGN:\n- Forearm cuff with handgrip\n- Opens laterally for quick release\n- Less bulky than axillary\n\nADVANTAGES:\n- No axillary pressure risk\n- Hands free with cuffs on\n- More mobility/maneuvering\n- Less conspicuous\n- Better for long-term use\n\nDISADVANTAGES:\n- Less stable than axillary\n- Requires better balance\n- More skill to use\n\nINDICATIONS:\n- Long-term crutch use\n- Permanent disability\n- Good balance and coordination\n- Examples: CP, polio, paraplegia\n\nFITTING:\n- Forearm cuff: 1-1.5 inches below elbow\n- Handgrip: At wrist crease/greater trochanter\n- Elbow flexion: 20-30 degrees\n- Cuff angle: 20-30 degrees from vertical',
