    back_text: 'WHEELCHAIR MEASUREMENTS:\n\nSEAT WIDTH:\n- Widest point of hips/thighs + 2 inches\n- Allow 1 inch each side\n- Too wide: Difficulty reaching wheels, poor posture\n- Too narrow: Pressure, discomfort\n\nSEAT DEPTH:\n- Posterior buttocks to popliteal fossa - 2-3 inches\n- Allow 2-3 inches from seat edge to popliteal\n- Too deep: Posterior pelvic tilt, pressure\n- Too shallow: Inadequate thigh support\n\nSEAT HEIGHT:\n- Thigh parallel to floor\n- Footrests: 2 inches minimum from floor\n- Consider cushion height\n\nBACK HEIGHT:\n- Inferior angle of scapula for self-propelling\n- Higher if need trunk support\n\nARMREST HEIGHT:\n- Elbow at 90 degrees\n- Shoulders relaxed',
    source_pdf_id: null,
    source_page_number: null,
