  {
    id: 'fc-equip-15',
    subcategory_id: 'equip-wheelchairs',
    front_text: 'What are common wheelchair positioning problems and solutions?',
    back_text: 'WHEELCHAIR POSITIONING PROBLEMS:\n\nPOSTERIOR PELVIC TILT:\n- Cause: Seat too deep, weak trunk\n- Effects: Sacral sitting, kyphosis, sliding\n- Solution: Wedge cushion, lumbar support, reduce depth\n\nANTERIOR PELVIC TILT:\n- Cause: Seat too shallow, hip flexor tightness\n- Solution: Increase seat depth, stretch hip flexors\n\nOBLIQUITY (Lateral tilt):\n- Cause: Scoliosis, asymmetric tone\n- Solution: Lateral trunk supports, contoured cushion\n\nWINDSWEPT DEFORMITY:\n- Cause: Spasticity, positioning\n- Both legs deviate to one side\n- Solution: Hip guides, knee separators\n\nSLIDING FORWARD:\n- Cause: Posterior tilt, smooth surface\n- Solution: Anti-thrust seat, seat belt, wedge\n\nPRESSURE RELIEF:\n- Weight shifts every 15-30 minutes\n- Appropriate cushion selection',
    source_pdf_id: null,
    source_page_number: null,
    tags: ['wheelchair', 'positioning'],
