    back_text: 'WHEELCHAIR CUSHION TYPES:\n\n1. FOAM CUSHIONS:\n- Least expensive\n- Lightweight\n- Limited pressure relief\n- Need replacement every 6-12 months\n- Low-risk patients\n\n2. GEL CUSHIONS:\n- Better pressure distribution\n- Heavier than foam\n- Can leak or bottom out\n- Moderate risk patients\n\n3. AIR CUSHIONS (ROHO):\n- Interconnected air cells\n- Excellent pressure relief\n- Require maintenance/inflation\n- High-risk patients\n- Example: SCI, severe pressure ulcer risk\n\n4. HONEYCOMB CUSHIONS:\n- Good pressure relief\n- Lightweight\n- No maintenance\n\n5. CUSTOM CONTOURED:\n- Molded to patient\n- Maximum support\n- Most expensive\n- Fixed deformities, complex needs\n\nSELECTION FACTORS:\n- Pressure relief needs\n- Postural support\n- Comfort\n- Weight\n- Maintenance ability',
