    back_text: 'KAFO (Knee-Ankle-Foot Orthosis):\n\nCOMPONENTS:\n- Thigh cuff\n- Knee joint (various types)\n- Calf band\n- AFO component\n\nKNEE JOINT OPTIONS:\n1. Locked (ring/drop lock): Maximum stability\n2. Offset: Stays extended with weight bearing\n3. Polycentric: Anatomical knee motion\n4. Stance control: Locks in stance, free in swing\n\nINDICATIONS:\n- Quadriceps weakness (<3/5 strength)\n- Knee instability (genu recurvatum)\n- Combined ankle and knee weakness\n- Polio/post-polio syndrome\n- SCI (low thoracic/lumbar)\n- Muscular dystrophy\n\nGAIT WITH KAFO:\n- High energy cost\n- Requires significant UE strength\n- Often needs crutches/walker\n- Circumduction or hip hiking common\n\nCONTRAINDICATIONS:\n- Hip flexion contracture >20 degrees\n- Severe obesity\n- Poor motivation',
