    front_text: 'What are the components of a transtibial (BKA) prosthesis?',
    back_text: 'TRANSTIBIAL PROSTHESIS COMPONENTS:\n\n1. SOCKET:\n- PTB (Patellar Tendon Bearing): Weight on patellar tendon\n- TSB (Total Surface Bearing): Weight distributed\n- Liner: Silicone, gel, or foam\n- Suspension: Pin lock, suction, sleeve\n\n2. PYLON/SHANK:\n- Endoskeletal: Foam cover over metal tube\n- Exoskeletal: Hard plastic shell\n\n3. FOOT/ANKLE:\n- SACH foot: Solid ankle cushion heel (basic)\n- Single-axis: Allows PF/DF\n- Multi-axis: Allows all planes\n- Dynamic response: Energy storing/returning\n- Microprocessor: Computerized (C-Leg foot)\n\nSOCKET FIT:\n- Pistoning: Socket too loose\n- Distal pressure: Socket too tight\n- Check tissue tolerance daily\n- Sock ply management\n\nALIGNMENT:\n- Proper knee alignment crucial\n- Affects gait and comfort',
