    back_text: 'TRANSFEMORAL PROSTHESIS COMPONENTS:\n\n1. SOCKET:\n- Quadrilateral: Ischial shelf, narrow ML\n- Ischial containment: Ischium inside socket\n- Subischial: Below ischium\n\n2. KNEE UNIT:\n- Single-axis: Basic, may buckle\n- Polycentric: Multiple pivot points, stable\n- Weight-activated: Locks with weight bearing\n- Manual locking: Locks with lever\n- Hydraulic: Resistance varies with speed\n- Microprocessor (C-Leg): Computer-controlled\n\n3. PYLON/SHANK\n\n4. FOOT/ANKLE (same as TT)\n\nSUSPENSION:\n- Suction\n- Pin/shuttle lock\n- Belt/strap\n- Vacuum-assisted\n\nALIGNMENT:\n- TKA line (trochanter-knee-ankle)\n- Knee stability critical\n- Hip musculature affects gait\n\nENERGY COST:\n- Higher than TT (40-65% above normal)\n- Prosthetic knee function critical',
