    front_text: 'What is residual limb care for amputees?',
    back_text: 'RESIDUAL LIMB CARE:\n\nHYGIENE:\n- Wash daily with mild soap\n- Rinse thoroughly\n- Dry completely\n- Inspect skin daily\n- Report any changes immediately\n\nSOCK/LINER CARE:\n- Wash daily\n- Air dry completely\n- Replace worn socks\n- Manage ply for fit\n\nEDEMA CONTROL:\n- Shrinker sock when not wearing prosthesis\n- Elastic wrap (figure-8)\n- Elevation initially\n- Avoid prolonged dependency\n\nPOSITIONING:\n- Avoid hip flexion contracture:\n  * Prone lying (TT and TF)\n  * No pillow under residual limb\n  * Avoid prolonged sitting\n- Avoid abduction contracture (TF)\n- Avoid knee flexion contracture (TT)\n\nPRESSURE AREAS:\n- Check distal end, bony prominences\n- Report redness lasting >20 min\n- Socket modifications may be needed',
