    front_text: 'What are ADA requirements for doorways and thresholds?',
    back_text: 'ADA DOORWAY REQUIREMENTS:\n\nCLEAR WIDTH:\n- Minimum: 32 inches (clear opening)\n- Preferred: 36 inches\n- Measured with door open 90 degrees\n\nMANEUVERING CLEARANCE:\n- Pull side (latch approach): 60 x 18 inches\n- Push side (latch approach): 48 x 0 inches\n- Front approach: 60 x 60 inches\n\nTHRESHOLD:\n- Maximum height: 1/2 inch\n- Beveled edge if >1/4 inch\n- Must be flush with floor surface\n\nHARDWARE:\n- Operable with one hand\n- No tight grasping or twisting\n- Lever handles preferred\n- Maximum operation height: 48 inches\n\nCLOSING SPEED:\n- Minimum 3 seconds from 70 to fully closed\n- 5 seconds for fire doors\n\nFORCE:\n- Maximum 5 lbf to open\n- Fire doors: Per fire code',
