  {
    id: 'fc-equip-28',
    subcategory_id: 'equip-orthotics',
    front_text: 'What are indications for an AFO based on muscle weakness?',
    back_text: 'AFO PRESCRIPTION BY MUSCLE WEAKNESS:\n\nDORSIFLEXOR WEAKNESS (Foot Drop):\n- PLS AFO (mild weakness)\n- Solid AFO (moderate-severe)\n- Provides toe clearance in swing\n\nPLANTARFLEXOR WEAKNESS:\n- May need AFO for push-off assist\n- Dynamic response AFO\n- Consider energy-storing foot\n\nINVERSION/EVERSION WEAKNESS:\n- Medial/lateral instability\n- Solid AFO or SMO\n- Lateral ankle support\n\nQUADRICEPS WEAKNESS:\n- Floor reaction AFO\n- Creates knee extension moment\n- Must have PF strength\n\nGENERAL PRINCIPLES:\n- Less is more - least restrictive that meets goals\n- Consider energy cost\n- Cosmetic concerns\n- Functional goals\n- Assess spasticity\n- Joint contractures limit options',
    source_pdf_id: null,
    source_page_number: null,
    tags: ['AFO', 'orthotic', 'muscle weakness'],
  },
  {
    id: 'fc-equip-29',
    subcategory_id: 'equip-wheelchairs',
    front_text: 'What are the types of manual wheelchairs?',
    back_text: 'MANUAL WHEELCHAIR TYPES:\n\n1. STANDARD/DEPOT:\n- Heavy, institutional\n- Not customized\n- Short-term use\n\n2. LIGHTWEIGHT:\n- 30-35 lbs\n- More adjustable\n- Better for daily use\n- Insurance typically covers\n\n3. ULTRA-LIGHTWEIGHT:\n- <30 lbs\n- Most customizable\n- Rigid or folding frame\n- Active users\n\n4. RIGID FRAME:\n- Non-folding\n- More efficient propulsion\n- Lighter weight\n- Better performance\n- Transport challenges\n\n5. FOLDING FRAME:\n- Cross-brace fold\n- Easier transport\n- Less efficient (energy lost in frame)\n\n6. TILT-IN-SPACE:\n- Seat tilts posteriorly\n- Maintains hip angle\n- Pressure relief\n- Dependent users\n\n7. RECLINING:\n- Back reclines\n- Hip angle changes\n- Pressure relief\n- Rest positioning',
    source_pdf_id: null,
    source_page_number: null,
