    back_text: 'PROSTHETIC TRAINING PROGRESSION:\n\nPHASE 1: PRE-PROSTHETIC:\n- Residual limb care/shaping\n- Edema control\n- ROM exercises\n- Strengthening (emphasis hip extensors, abductors)\n- Transfers\n- Mobility without prosthesis\n- Contracture prevention\n\nPHASE 2: PROSTHETIC TRAINING:\n- Donning/doffing\n- Skin inspection\n- Weight shifting in parallel bars\n- Standing balance\n- Weight transfer to prosthetic side\n- Stepping in place\n\nPHASE 3: GAIT TRAINING:\n- Parallel bars\n- Walker/crutches\n- Progression to cane\n- Even surfaces\n- Uneven terrain\n- Stairs and ramps\n- Community mobility\n\nPHASE 4: ADVANCED:\n- Fall recovery\n- Running (if appropriate)\n- Sports-specific\n- Vocational activities',
    source_pdf_id: null,
