  {
    id: 'fc-equip-32',
    subcategory_id: 'equip-orthotics',
    front_text: 'What are common orthotic gait deviations?',
    back_text: 'ORTHOTIC GAIT DEVIATIONS:\n\nWITH AFO:\n\nExcessive Knee Flexion (Stance):\n- AFO set in too much dorsiflexion\n- Heel too high on shoe\n\nGenu Recurvatum:\n- AFO set in too much plantarflexion\n- Heel too low\n- Weak quads\n\nLateral Trunk Lean:\n- Poor medial-lateral control\n- Weak hip abductors\n\nCircumduction:\n- AFO too long (blocking DF)\n- Prosthetic/orthotic too long\n\nWITH KAFO:\n\nHip Hiking:\n- Compensate for locked knee\n- Device too long\n\nCircumduction:\n- Clear locked knee in swing\n\nVaulting:\n- Rise on sound side toe\n- Device too long\n\nTrunk Lean:\n- Poor hip control\n- Compensate for device weight',
    source_pdf_id: null,
