    id: 'fc-equip-33',
    subcategory_id: 'equip-gait',
    front_text: 'How do you calculate crutch/walker height?',
    back_text: 'ASSISTIVE DEVICE HEIGHT CALCULATIONS:\n\nAXILLARY CRUTCHES:\nStanding method:\n- 2-3 finger widths below axilla\n- Tips 4-6 inches lateral, 2 inches anterior\n\nSupine method:\n- Length = height - 16 inches\n- OR anterior axillary fold to heel + 2 inches\n\nHandgrip: Greater trochanter OR wrist crease\n\nLOFSTRAND CRUTCHES:\n- Handgrip at greater trochanter/wrist crease\n- Forearm cuff 1-1.5 inches below olecranon\n\nCANES:\n- Top at greater trochanter\n- OR wrist crease when standing\n\nWALKERS:\n- Top at wrist crease\n- OR greater trochanter level\n\nALL DEVICES:\n- Elbow flexion: 20-30 degrees\n- Check on level surface\n- Patient wearing usual shoes',
    source_pdf_id: null,
