  {
    id: 'fc-equip-34',
    subcategory_id: 'equip-weight-bearing',
    front_text: 'What devices are appropriate for each weight bearing status?',
    back_text: 'WEIGHT BEARING STATUS & DEVICE SELECTION:\n\nNON-WEIGHT BEARING (NWB):\n- Walker: 3-point gait\n- Axillary crutches: 3-point\n- Platform walker (if cannot grip)\n- Wheelchair for distances\n\nTOE TOUCH/TOUCH DOWN (TTWB):\n- Walker: Modified 3-point\n- Crutches: 3-point\n- May progress to cane when allowed PWB\n\nPARTIAL WEIGHT BEARING (PWB):\n- Walker or crutches: 3-point\n- May use bathroom scale to practice\n- Progress device as WB increases\n\nWEIGHT BEARING AS TOLERATED (WBAT):\n- Walker, crutches, or cane\n- Device based on balance, strength\n- May not need device if stable\n\nFULL WEIGHT BEARING (FWB):\n- May use device for safety/confidence\n- Progress to no device when ready\n- Consider terrain, endurance\n\nKEY: Match device to patient abilities AND weight bearing restrictions',
    source_pdf_id: null,
