    back_text: 'PROSTHETIC FOOT TYPES:\n\n1. SACH (Solid Ankle Cushion Heel):\n- Simplest, most durable\n- Cushioned heel compresses at heel strike\n- No ankle motion\n- Low activity level (K1-K2)\n\n2. SINGLE-AXIS:\n- Allows plantarflexion/dorsiflexion\n- Bumpers limit motion\n- Adds stability at heel strike\n- K1-K2 activity\n\n3. MULTI-AXIS:\n- Motion in all planes\n- Adapts to uneven surfaces\n- Good for outdoor/varied terrain\n- K2-K3 activity\n\n4. DYNAMIC RESPONSE (Energy Storing):\n- Flexible keel stores/returns energy\n- Push-off assist\n- More natural gait\n- K3-K4 activity (active)\n\n5. MICROPROCESSOR:\n- Computer-controlled\n- Adjusts to terrain/speed\n- Most natural gait\n- Highest activity level (K3-K4)\n- Most expensive',
