    front_text: 'What are wheelchair propulsion techniques and efficiency?',
    back_text: 'WHEELCHAIR PROPULSION:\n\nPROPULSION PATTERNS:\n1. Semicircular: Hand follows arc\n2. Single looping: Drop below wheel\n3. Double looping: Figure-8 pattern\n4. Arc: Short strokes, hands near top\n\nMOST EFFICIENT:\n- Semicircular pattern\n- Long, smooth strokes\n- Minimal strokes per distance\n- Hands drop below push rim on recovery\n\nWHEEL POSITION:\n- Axle position affects propulsion\n- More forward axle = easier propulsion\n- More forward = less stable (tips easier)\n- Balance efficiency vs. stability\n\nERGONOMICS:\n- Shoulder injury common\n- Proper setup crucial\n- Consider power assist\n- Shoulder exercises/flexibility\n\nGRADES/RAMPS:\n- Lean forward going up\n- Control descent\n- May need assistance\n- Consider power wheelchair for steep/long ramps',
